## Unix vs Linux

| Feature | UNIX | Linux |
|---|---|---|
| Origin | 1970s, AT&T Bell Labs | 1991, Linus Torvalds |
| Source Code | Closed-source | Open-source |
| Cost | Paid | Free (mostly) |
| Flexibility | Limited | Highly customizable |
| Examples | AIX, HP-UX, Solaris | Ubuntu, RHEL, CentOS |
| Primary Use | Enterprise servers | Servers, desktops, cloud |

> **Key Point:** Linux is not UNIX — it is *Unix-like* (POSIX compliant). They share design philosophy, not code.

