## What is Firmware?

Firmware is low-level software stored in hardware (ROM/Flash memory) that initializes the system before the OS loads.

**Examples:** BIOS, UEFI, router firmware

| Component | Role |
|---|---|
| Firmware (BIOS/UEFI) | Starts the system |
| Bootloader (GRUB) | Loads the OS |
| Kernel | Runs the OS |

**Low-level vs High-level software:**

| Feature | Low-Level | High-Level |
|---|---|---|
| Interaction | Direct with hardware | Through the OS |
| Examples | Firmware, kernel, device drivers | Browsers, applications |

