## DOS vs Linux Terminal

| Feature | DOS (Command Prompt) | Linux Terminal |
|---|---|---|
| OS Type | Single-user | Multi-user |
| Commands | Basic | Advanced |
| Scripting | Limited | Very powerful (bash scripts) |
| File System | Simple (C:, D:) | Hierarchical (single root `/`) |
| Security | Weak | Strong |
| Primary Use | Personal PC | Servers, cloud, DevOps |

**Path separator:**
- Linux: `/` (forward slash) — e.g., `/home/ziya/file.txt`
- DOS/Windows: `\` (backslash) — e.g., `C:\Users\ziya\file.txt`

